UID:f7225fde69503fe7@role-estate-probate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260810T191408Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260810
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Intensive Outpatient Program (IOP) Clinical E
 ligibility Review and Billing Criteria for Section 45 and 46 Hospitals Upd
 ate
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Intensive Outpatient Program (IOP) Clinical Eligibility
  Review and Billing Criteria for Section 45 and 46 Hospitals Update\nInten
 sive Outpatient Program (IOP) Clinical Eligibility Review and Billing Crit
 eria for Section 45 and 46 Hospitals Update\nAug 10\, 2026\nBeginning Sept
 ember 1\, 2026\, IOP services delivered by hospitals enrolled under Mai
 neCare Benefits Manual (MBM) Chapter II\, Sections 45 and 46 will require
  clinical eligibility review and billing criteria in alignment with Medica
 re’s IOP services billing requirements.\nEffective for dates of service 
 on\, or after\, September 1\, 2026\, hospitals delivering IOP services m
 ust:\nSubmit a clinical review request to Acentra Health before deliv
 ering services to determine a MaineCare member’s IOP service eligib
 ility. Members determined to meet clinical eligibility criteria as defined
  in MBM\, Chapter II\, Section 65 will receive a Case ID number to authori
 ze billing for the delivery of IOP services by Section 45 and 46 providers
 .\nWith clinical review approval\, deliver IOP services in accordance wit
 h their hospital licensure and the requirements of MBM\, Chapter II\, Sec
 tion 65.05-4.\nSubmit claims using the corresponding CPT/HCPCS codes or r
 evenue codes for actual services delivered including modifier(s) as appli
 cable. Condition Code 92 (CC 92) is required in Form Locator fields 18-2
 4.\nRetain the clinical review Case ID number in the member’s medical re
 cord. Because IOP services without a clinical review Case ID are not eligi
 ble for reimbursement\, providers must maintain clinical review approval
  records for Program Integrity purposes.\nDeliver services in accordance 
 with Division of Licensing and Certification (DLC) requirements.\nPlease 
 note: This notice supersedes previous MaineCare Section 45 and 46 IOP 
 billing instructions including\, but not limited to\, the\nJune 14\, 2023
 \nand\nAugust 18\, 2023\nmessa\nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/p
 rovider-bulletins/intensive-outpatient-program-iop-clinical-eligibility-re
 view-and-billing-criteria-section
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/intensive-
 outpatient-program-iop-clinical-eligibility-review-and-billing-criteria-se
 ction
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:d77d1fdf1d0bec33@role-estate-probate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260810T191408Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260810
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Stakeholder Group Meeting: Nursing Facility R
 eform Transition Fund
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Stakeholder Group Meeting: Nursing Facility Reform Tran
 sition Fund\nStakeholder Group Meeting: Nursing Facility Reform Transition
  Fund\nAug 10\, 2026\nPursuant to\nResolve 2025\, Chapter 157\nthe Depart
 ment of Health and Human Services is convening a group to examine the us
 e of the Nursing Facility Reform Transition Fund\, established under\nP.
 L. 2023\, Chapter 643\, Part SSS\n. The first meeting will be held on 
 August 31\, 2026 at 3:00 PM through Zoom. Meetings are open to the pub
 lic.\nRegister\nfor the Zoom meeting.\nThe group must submit a report to
  the Maine Legislature’s Joint Standing Committee on Health and Human Se
 rvices no later than January 15\, 2027\, addressing the following:\nNursin
 g Facility Reform Transition Fund expenses to date\;\nPlan for spending th
 e remaining funds\;\nCycle for rebasing reimbursement rates\; and\nUse of 
 the fund to pay for cost-of-living increases for staff pay compared with
  the use of other funding sources for other cost-of-living increases fo
 r direct care services.\nFor questions\, please contact LTSS Initiative
 s Manager\nAmanda Nelson\n\, or Deputy Director of Policy and Programs\nO
 livia Alford\n.\nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulleti
 ns/stakeholder-group-meeting-nursing-facility-reform-transition-fund-2026-
 08-10
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/stakeholde
 r-group-meeting-nursing-facility-reform-transition-fund-2026-08-10
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
