BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:79e3d8a3e19d6408@role-estate-probate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260807T001402Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260806
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Addition of the TH Modifier to Support Nation
 al Maternity Care Coding and Reimbursement Changes Effective September 1\,
  2026
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Addition of the TH Modifier to Support National Materni
 ty Care Coding and Reimbursement Changes Effective September 1\, 2026\nAdd
 ition of the TH Modifier to Support National Maternity Care Coding and Rei
 mbursement Changes Effective September 1\, 2026\nAug 06\, 2026\nThe\nAmeri
 can Medical Association (AMA) announced maternity care services code chan
 ges\nthat will be effective January 1\, 2027. These changes include the re
 moval of\n17\nbilling codes\, the addition of 12 billing codes\, and revis
 ions to 6 billing codes to reflect modern obstetric practices\, allow for 
 more accurate and transparent reporting\, and to create a data foundation 
 to better attribute maternal care and support the complexities of team-bas
 ed care throughout a patient's journey.\nIn preparation for these changes\
 , MaineCare is also making changes to coding requirements for maternity ca
 re services\, including the transition to non-global and non-bundled care 
 coding and reimbursement. To ensure consistent reimbursement MaineCare is 
 directing providers to take the following actions no later than prior to S
 eptember 1\, 2026:\nAdjust maternity care visit billing from global or bun
 dled service codes to Evaluation and Management (E/M) service codes based 
 on each member’s estimated due date and the anticipated number of visits
  for the remainder of their antepartum period in accordance with\nAMA Ante
 partum Transition Reporting guidance\;\n.\nAppend the TH modifier for all 
 maternity care E/M service codes on your claim to identify the visit as a 
 maternity care service\;\nTransition from total-visit tracking to individu
 al encounter documentation\, as each prenatal and postpartum visit must no
 w independently support standard E/M complexity or time rules\; and\nMonit
 or professional guidance from organizations like the American College of O
 bstetrics and Gynecology and the AMA to prepare billers and systems\nhttps
 ://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/addition-th-modifie
 r-support-national-maternity-care-coding-and-reimbursement-changes
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/addition-t
 h-modifier-support-national-maternity-care-coding-and-reimbursement-change
 s
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
